{
  "_readme": "EXAMPLE production mapping. Column names, codes, formats and paths below are illustrative placeholders, not Humana's real data dictionary: they show the shape the mapping takes. Before the first production run, the data owner for each feed replaces them with the real extract layout (see docs/DATA_REQUEST.md), and tests/test_v3_production.py is rerun against a sample extract. Months may arrive as YYYYMM integers; codes are mapped explicitly so an unexpected code stops the run instead of being dropped. Month formats: CSV and integer months use a strftime format such as %Y%m; a native Parquet DATE or TIMESTAMP column arrives as text like 2025-07-01 and must be mapped with %Y-%m-%d.",
